post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> Argus installed.

Argus runs as a per-user systemd --user service. This package ships a
global enablement symlink, so the service is ALREADY enabled and will
start automatically on your next graphical login — no manual
`systemctl --user enable` needed.

To start it immediately in the current session without logging out:

    argus service start

The tray icon (etc/xdg/autostart/argus-tray.desktop) will start
automatically on your next graphical login. To start it immediately this
session, run: argus tray &

FIRST SCREEN CAPTURE: on KDE Plasma / Wayland, the first time Argus
grabs a screenshot it will trigger a one-time system consent dialog from
xdg-desktop-portal (the ScreenCast picker). Approve it once; subsequent
captures are silent. If you dismiss/deny it, screen capture will keep
re-prompting or silently failing — re-run and accept to fix.

VISION / NARRATIVES: on-demand vision narratives (used by `argus report
daily --vision` / `--weekly --vision`) require a Gemini API key in the
environment as GEMINI_API_KEY (or GOOGLE_API_KEY) — Argus never reads or
stores this key in its own config file. Since the systemd --user service
does not inherit your interactive shell's environment, set it where a
systemd user unit will actually pick it up, e.g.:

    mkdir -p ~/.config/environment.d
    echo 'GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here' >> ~/.config/environment.d/argus.conf
    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    systemctl --user restart argus.service

Without a key, everything else (capture, dashboard, retention, reports
without --vision) works fine — vision narratives are opt-in only.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> Argus upgraded.

If this upgrade bumped Arch's `python` package across a major/minor
version (not just a patch release), Argus's bundled venv interpreter
under /opt/argus/venv may now be ABI-mismatched against
--system-site-packages providers like python-gobject. See the PKGBUILD's
top-of-file comment for details. If the tray icon or screen capture stop
working after a `python` upgrade, reinstall this package
(`makepkg -f` + reinstall, once a rebuilt package is available) rather
than filing it as an Argus bug.

Pick up the new version now (or just log out and back in):
    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    systemctl --user restart argus.service
EOF
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> Argus removed.

The systemd --user unit and autostart entry were removed with the
package, but this does NOT stop an already-running instance for users
who are currently logged in — if Argus is still running, stop it
yourself:

    systemctl --user disable --now argus.service

Your data (SQLite DB + captured images under ~/.local/share/argus/) and
config (~/.config/argus/config.toml) are left in place — remove them by
hand if you want a full wipe.
EOF
}
